; parse_date_mask_routine formats each parsed date back and compares it
; with the input.  That round trip is what rejects text strptime leaves
; unconsumed after a complete date; out-of-range months and days are
; rejected by strptime itself, and impossible days such as Feb 30 by
; Boost.Date (see cov-times-invalid-date.test).  These blocks pin the
; trailing text the round trip rejects; date-round-trip-trailing-text.test
; pins the dates it accepts.

2024/01/05 Payee
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Assets:Cash

test eval [2024/01/05x] --now 2030/06/15 -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing value expression:
  [2024/01/05x]

Error: Invalid date: 2024/01/05x
end test

test eval [01/05x] --now 2030/06/15 -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing value expression:
  [01/05x]

Error: Invalid date: 01/05x
end test

test eval [2024-01-05x] --input-date-format '%Y-%m-%d' --now 2030/06/15 -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing value expression:
  [2024-01-05x]

Error: Invalid date: 2024-01-05x
end test
